1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,581
There was a time a farm got
found by the sign on the road.

2
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:06,398
Today it gets found on
a phone. In a kitchen.

3
00:00:06,418 --> 00:00:08,602
Before anyone picks up the car keys.

4
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:10,611
Here's a number that should worry you.

5
00:00:10,631 --> 00:00:15,156
A national survey asked US farms that
welcome visitors how they market.

6
00:00:15,176 --> 00:00:17,908
The big two were social
media and word of mouth.

7
00:00:18,983 --> 00:00:22,594
No other marketing tool was
used by even half of them.

8
00:00:22,883 --> 00:00:26,118
So if you want to get your
farm on Google Maps, for free,

9
00:00:26,138 --> 00:00:27,570
this video is for you.

10
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,165
Without paying for ads.

11
00:00:29,185 --> 00:00:30,351
Without a website.

12
00:00:30,371 --> 00:00:32,552
And without being good with computers.

13
00:00:32,817 --> 00:00:34,581
Maybe there's a quiet voice saying,

14
00:00:34,601 --> 00:00:36,987
"Who would ever look
for a farm like mine?"

15
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:39,439
Somebody already is.

16
00:00:39,717 --> 00:00:40,750
In this video,

17
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:43,879
we will see why good
farms go invisible online,

18
00:00:43,899 --> 00:00:46,780
visit a family dairy that
learned it the hard way,

19
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,422
and walk through the
free fix in three steps.

20
00:00:49,683 --> 00:00:50,921
Stay for number three.

21
00:00:50,941 --> 00:00:52,758
It's the step most farmers skip,

22
00:00:52,778 --> 00:00:54,498
and it's where the visitors are.

23
00:00:54,783 --> 00:00:56,725
I'm Sarah. Yes, I'm a cartoon.

24
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:58,592
This channel comes from Stephen Loke,

25
00:00:58,612 --> 00:01:02,708
a durian farmer in Malaysia who
welcomes visitors to his farm.

26
00:01:03,883 --> 00:01:05,603
Here's the enemy. It isn't you.

27
00:01:05,623 --> 00:01:06,892
You're farming right.

28
00:01:07,183 --> 00:01:09,229
The enemy is being invisible.

29
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:12,424
Picture a family planning
their Saturday. They type,

30
00:01:12,444 --> 00:01:14,955
pick your own near me. Up comes a map.

31
00:01:15,217 --> 00:01:17,136
Some farms show smiling faces,

32
00:01:17,156 --> 00:01:19,139
opening hours, a phone number.

33
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:22,390
Then there's a gray pin.
No photos. No hours.

34
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:25,057
Maybe a name somebody
else typed in years ago.

35
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:27,495
Which one would you drive an hour for?

36
00:01:28,583 --> 00:01:29,670
That's the ghost pin.

37
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:30,863
And the hard part is,

38
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:33,524
many farm owners don't
even know it's there.

39
00:01:33,817 --> 00:01:36,502
So here's the big idea
I want you to remember.

40
00:01:36,522 --> 00:01:38,181
Your farm has two gates.

41
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:40,015
The first gate is on your road.

42
00:01:40,035 --> 00:01:41,827
You open it every morning.

43
00:01:42,117 --> 00:01:43,796
The second gate is on a phone,

44
00:01:43,816 --> 00:01:45,647
in a kitchen forty miles away.

45
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:48,410
That's where people decide
whether to come at all.

46
00:01:48,683 --> 00:01:52,459
Most farmers open the first gate
and leave the second one locked.

47
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:53,907
Call it the Second Gate.

48
00:01:53,927 --> 00:01:55,493
And opening it is free.

49
00:01:55,783 --> 00:01:58,714
Google says its local
results rest on three things.

50
00:01:58,734 --> 00:02:00,410
How well you match the search.

51
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:01,578
How far away you are.

52
00:02:01,598 --> 00:02:03,162
And how well known you are.

53
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:04,641
You can't move your farm.

54
00:02:04,661 --> 00:02:06,704
But the other two are in your hands.

55
00:02:07,883 --> 00:02:09,142
Fairbury, Illinois.

56
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:10,379
Nineteen fifty-eight.

57
00:02:10,399 --> 00:02:12,669
Duane and Arlene Kilgus start a dairy.

58
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:14,256
For more than thirty years,

59
00:02:14,276 --> 00:02:17,611
they sell their milk the way
most farmers do. To a co-op.

60
00:02:17,631 --> 00:02:19,087
At the co-op's price.

61
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:21,720
But the family wanted more
than the co-op's price.

62
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,715
Therefore they did something bold.

63
00:02:23,735 --> 00:02:27,261
They started bottling their own
Jersey milk, right on the farm.

64
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:28,881
They sold it to stores,

65
00:02:28,901 --> 00:02:31,572
restaurants and coffee
shops up in Chicago.

66
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:32,928
And in twenty oh nine,

67
00:02:32,948 --> 00:02:35,321
they opened a little
country store on the farm,

68
00:02:35,341 --> 00:02:36,895
a mile south of town.

69
00:02:37,983 --> 00:02:39,895
Then came spring twenty twenty.

70
00:02:40,183 --> 00:02:41,442
The restaurants closed.

71
00:02:41,462 --> 00:02:44,581
The family supplied about
two dozen of them in Chicago.

72
00:02:44,601 --> 00:02:46,985
And most of those
customers shut their doors,

73
00:02:47,005 --> 00:02:48,299
at least for a while.

74
00:02:48,583 --> 00:02:50,357
Therefore the family cut the herd,

75
00:02:50,377 --> 00:02:54,726
from about a hundred and fifty cows
to a hundred and fifteen. And still,

76
00:02:54,746 --> 00:02:55,878
it wasn't enough.

77
00:02:55,898 --> 00:02:58,259
Some of the milk had to
be dumped in the field.

78
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:01,739
Picture it. Fresh milk
from cows you raised.

79
00:03:01,759 --> 00:03:03,182
Poured onto the grass.

80
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,314
But one part of the farm kept going.

81
00:03:06,334 --> 00:03:07,934
That little country store.

82
00:03:08,217 --> 00:03:09,327
During the pandemic,

83
00:03:09,347 --> 00:03:11,129
more people came through its door.

84
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:14,122
And a steady crowd of
customers still comes today.

85
00:03:14,383 --> 00:03:16,883
Why? Because people knew
where that gate was.

86
00:03:16,903 --> 00:03:18,219
When the trucks stopped coming,

87
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:21,147
the customers who could
find the farm kept coming.

88
00:03:21,417 --> 00:03:24,668
Here's the lesson. You don't get
found in the middle of a crisis.

89
00:03:24,688 --> 00:03:26,219
You get found before it.

90
00:03:26,483 --> 00:03:29,427
If you're wondering what to
offer once people find you,

91
00:03:29,447 --> 00:03:31,158
Stephen created a free ebook,

92
00:03:31,178 --> 00:03:34,863
One Hundred Fifty Ways to Unlock
Hidden Wealth From Your Farm.

93
00:03:34,883 --> 00:03:36,721
The link is in the description.

94
00:03:36,741 --> 00:03:38,191
More about it at the end.

95
00:03:38,483 --> 00:03:40,573
And if this is helping, subscribe,

96
00:03:40,593 --> 00:03:42,588
so the next farm lesson finds you.

97
00:03:43,750 --> 00:03:45,039
Now, what this is not.

98
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:46,320
This isn't paid ads.

99
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:47,958
It isn't dancing on TikTok.

100
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:51,846
And it isn't a marketing agency
sending you a bill every month.

101
00:03:52,117 --> 00:03:56,372
In fact, Google says you can't pay for
a better spot in its local results.

102
00:03:56,392 --> 00:03:57,577
The spot is earned.

103
00:03:57,597 --> 00:03:59,324
And the tool to earn it is free.

104
00:03:59,617 --> 00:04:03,719
It's called a Google Business Profile.
Here's the fix, in three steps.

105
00:04:04,883 --> 00:04:07,055
Step number one. Find your pin.

106
00:04:07,317 --> 00:04:08,316
Take out your phone.

107
00:04:08,336 --> 00:04:09,677
Open Google Maps.

108
00:04:09,697 --> 00:04:10,803
Type your farm's name,

109
00:04:10,823 --> 00:04:12,130
the one on your sign.

110
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:13,793
Now look. Is there a pin?

111
00:04:13,813 --> 00:04:15,058
Is it in the right place?

112
00:04:15,078 --> 00:04:16,221
Are the hours right?

113
00:04:16,241 --> 00:04:18,081
Is that even your phone number?

114
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:21,541
Sometimes Google already
has a listing for your farm,

115
00:04:21,561 --> 00:04:23,183
built from what it found online,

116
00:04:23,203 --> 00:04:25,083
or one a visitor suggested.

117
00:04:25,103 --> 00:04:27,651
You might be on the map
and not even know it.

118
00:04:27,917 --> 00:04:30,185
If there's no pin at all, that's fine too.

119
00:04:30,205 --> 00:04:32,172
You'll make one in step number two.

120
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:34,900
Step number two. Claim it,

121
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,235
and prove it's yours.

122
00:04:36,517 --> 00:04:38,560
Go to business dot google dot com.

123
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,383
Sign in with a Google account.

124
00:04:40,403 --> 00:04:42,362
Search for your farm, and claim it.

125
00:04:42,382 --> 00:04:43,556
If there's no listing,

126
00:04:43,576 --> 00:04:45,631
add your farm as a new business.

127
00:04:45,917 --> 00:04:47,881
It costs nothing. Not a cent.

128
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:50,262
Then Google asks you to
prove you're the owner.

129
00:04:50,282 --> 00:04:53,150
It may offer a phone
call, a text, an email,

130
00:04:53,170 --> 00:04:55,209
or a short video. For a video,

131
00:04:55,229 --> 00:04:57,071
you film your sign, your farm,

132
00:04:57,091 --> 00:04:58,953
and something only the owner has,

133
00:04:58,973 --> 00:05:01,328
like the key to your
store or your farm tools.

134
00:05:01,348 --> 00:05:03,379
Just follow the steps it gives you.

135
00:05:03,650 --> 00:05:06,063
One warning. Use your farm's real name.

136
00:05:06,083 --> 00:05:07,226
The one on your sign.

137
00:05:07,246 --> 00:05:10,693
Google's rules say extra keywords
don't belong in the name,

138
00:05:10,713 --> 00:05:13,726
and adding them can get
your listing suspended.

139
00:05:14,917 --> 00:05:15,988
Step number three.

140
00:05:16,008 --> 00:05:17,768
The one I told you to stay for.

141
00:05:17,788 --> 00:05:19,159
Fill every box.

142
00:05:19,450 --> 00:05:21,328
This is the step most farmers skip.

143
00:05:21,348 --> 00:05:24,257
They claim the listing,
feel good, and walk away.

144
00:05:24,277 --> 00:05:25,861
And the pin stays a ghost.

145
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:28,294
Google says when a profile is complete,

146
00:05:28,314 --> 00:05:32,824
people are two point seven times more
likely to see the business as reputable.

147
00:05:32,844 --> 00:05:35,406
And seventy percent more likely to visit.

148
00:05:35,683 --> 00:05:37,080
So here's what to fill in.

149
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,342
Your main category.

150
00:05:38,362 --> 00:05:40,053
Choose what visitors come to do,

151
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:41,273
not only what you grow.

152
00:05:41,293 --> 00:05:43,059
Type something like, pick your own,

153
00:05:43,079 --> 00:05:44,927
and see what Google suggests.

154
00:05:45,217 --> 00:05:47,640
Your real hours. If
you're seasonal, say so.

155
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,276
Mark the days you're closed.

156
00:05:49,550 --> 00:05:51,191
Photos of people having fun.

157
00:05:51,211 --> 00:05:52,561
Kids feeding the goats.

158
00:05:52,581 --> 00:05:54,406
A family at the picnic table.

159
00:05:54,426 --> 00:05:55,837
Not just your crops.

160
00:05:56,117 --> 00:05:57,944
Your phone number and how to book.

161
00:05:57,964 --> 00:06:01,493
And a few plain sentences
about what a visit feels like.

162
00:06:01,783 --> 00:06:05,976
That's the Second Gate, unlocked.
Same farm. Same road. But now,

163
00:06:05,996 --> 00:06:08,053
when that family in the kitchen searches,

164
00:06:08,073 --> 00:06:10,055
your farm shows up with a face.

165
00:06:11,217 --> 00:06:12,765
Maybe you're thinking, "Sarah,

166
00:06:12,785 --> 00:06:15,077
my farm is too remote for any of this."

167
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:18,556
Here's the truth. Remote
is exactly why you need it.

168
00:06:18,817 --> 00:06:21,772
Nobody drives past a
remote farm by accident.

169
00:06:21,792 --> 00:06:24,394
Every single visitor
will look you up first.

170
00:06:24,414 --> 00:06:25,787
If the Second Gate is locked,

171
00:06:25,807 --> 00:06:28,030
the trip ends right there, in the kitchen.

172
00:06:28,317 --> 00:06:29,446
And if you're thinking,

173
00:06:29,466 --> 00:06:30,935
"I'm no good with computers,"

174
00:06:30,955 --> 00:06:35,745
USDA figures show eighty-two percent
of American farms have a smartphone.

175
00:06:35,765 --> 00:06:37,981
If you can send a photo to your grandkids,

176
00:06:38,001 --> 00:06:39,251
you can do this.

177
00:06:40,417 --> 00:06:41,956
Remember that sign on the road?

178
00:06:41,976 --> 00:06:43,172
It still matters.

179
00:06:43,192 --> 00:06:45,159
But today it's only the first gate.

180
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:49,407
The Kilgus family's store kept going
because people knew where to find it.

181
00:06:49,427 --> 00:06:51,248
Your farm deserves the same.

182
00:06:52,317 --> 00:06:54,943
Watching this won't change
anything. Doing will.

183
00:06:55,217 --> 00:06:56,927
So here's your homework. Today,

184
00:06:56,947 --> 00:06:59,077
search your farm's name on Google Maps.

185
00:06:59,097 --> 00:07:02,731
Then tell me in the comments what
you found. Nothing? A ghost pin?

186
00:07:02,751 --> 00:07:03,971
Or a full listing?

187
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:05,840
And once people can find you,

188
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,293
give them a reason to come.

189
